WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
I need 100 prints in three days. I still control the purchase.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Agents propose. Vowrail’s gateway enforces spending permission.

3
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:18.000
The buyer allows USD 220 and two negotiation rounds.

4
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Sellers receive public requirements, never the private ceiling.

5
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:29.000
Two rounds means two. The gateway refuses another.

6
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:34.000
Invented offers and above-budget checkout are blocked.

7
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:41.000
Choose a stored offer. Delivery, tax and refund terms still need review.

8
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Order creation, buyer approval and capture are separate.

9
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:56.000
Expired permission blocks checkout or capture. This is a synthetic expiry replay.

10
00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:02.000
An earlier separate Sandbox run completed one authorized USD 207 purchase.

11
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:08.000
Amount and currency matched. The synthetic seller was not the configured payee.

12
00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:13.000
When a response is uncertain, check the stored outcome without another capture.

13
00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:18.000
Earlier restart restored the completed receipt after expiry.

14
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:24.000
AI helps. Your permission stays explicit and the result stays checkable.

15
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:30.000
Model explanations remain unverified. Evidence comes from separate runs. Private review only.
